#X text 45 88 [playlist~] is a soundfile player with a playlist. The waveform of the loaded file is drawn across the top with a play/pause button on its left \, and the files are listed underneath. Click a row to load that file \, click or drag the waveform to scrub \, and click the button to start or pause., f 66;
#X obj 375 162 else/playlist~;
#X obj 375 363 else/out~;
#X obj 45 162 loadbang;
#X msg 45 188 add bagal.flac dholak.flac drum-loop.flac sax.wav, f 24;
#X msg 45 232 select 0;
#X msg 112 232 select 2;
#X msg 45 257 play 1;
#X msg 105 257 play 0;
#X msg 45 282 pos 0;
#X msg 100 282 pos 0.5;
#X msg 45 307 remove 0;
#X msg 118 307 clear;
#N canvas 103 54 1438 875 interface 0;
#X text 30 20 The object is split in two. The upper strip is the transport: the button on the left starts and pauses playback \, and the rest of it is the waveform of the file that is loaded. Clicking or dragging anywhere in the waveform moves the play position \, and a line marks where playback is., f 64;
#X text 30 90 The lower part is the playlist itself \, one row per file \, numbered from 0 Click a row to load it \, which also stops playback and rewinds to the start. Long names are cut off with an ellipsis., f 64;
#X text 30 150 When there are more files than fit \, a scrollbar appears on the right: the arrows step one row \, dragging the bar jumps and dragging the list itself scrolls it., f 64;
#X text 30 205 The object is graph-on-parent at a fixed 300 by 190 pixels. Note that the same clicks that drive the GUI are also what the 'select' \, 'play' and 'pos' messages do \, so you can drive it either way., f 64;
#X obj 299 382 else/playlist~;
#X obj 31 271 loadbang;
#X msg 31 296 add bagal.flac dholak.flac drum-loop.flac sax.wav voice.wav baglama.wav didge.flac violin.flac kantele.flac vacuous.flac, f 30;
#X obj 299 582 else/out~;
#X text 30 420 ten files \, so the list scrolls;
#X connect 4 0 7 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 0 4 0;
#X restore 45 367 pd interface;
#N canvas 34 78 1612 970 example 0;
#X text 30 20 The outlet is a multichannel signal with 16 channels \, so files of up to 16 channels play back as they are. Use [nchs~] to see the count and [else/select~] or [snake~ out] to pick channels out of it., f 64;
#X text 30 80 Here the playlist feeds a reverb. The files are found the same way Pd finds any other file \, so these load from ELSE's own folder \; your own files can sit next to the patch., f 64;
#X obj 30 200 else/playlist~;
#X obj 30 145 loadbang;
#X msg 30 170 add bagal.flac dholak.flac drum-loop.flac, f 30;
